+# Implementation Plan: JSON Pointer Resolution
+
+**Branch**: `001-json-pointer` | **Date**: 2026-10-21 | **Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Add `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` implementing RFC 6901 string form. The pointer is split into reference tokens, validated and unescaped by a small internal parser (reusable by later features), then walked through the document with strict object/array rules. Every failure throws an `Error`.
+
+## Technical Context
+
+**Language/Version**: TypeScript (ES2022, strict, NodeNext modules)
+**Primary Dependencies**: none (runtime dependency-free, per README)
+**Storage**: N/A
+**Testing**: `node --test` (npm test); Node 22 runs `.ts` tests natively (type stripping); see research.md
+**Target Platform**: Node.js library
+**Project Type**: library
+**Performance Goals**: linear in pointer length
+**Constraints**: no mutation of document; no runtime dependencies
+**Scale/Scope**: one function plus an internal token parser
+
+## Constitution Check
+
+The constitution file is an unfilled template: no ratified principles apply. Governing constraints taken from README: no runtime dependency; behaviour must follow the published standard (RFC 6901). Gate: pass.
+
+## Project Structure
+
+```text
+specs/001-json-pointer/   # spec, plan, research, data-model, contracts, quickstart, tasks
+src/
+└── index.ts              # parsePointer (internal) + resolvePointer (exported)
+test/
+└── pointer.test.ts       # RFC examples and error cases (run by node --test, native TS stripping)
+```
+
+**Structure Decision**: single-project library; kept in `src/index.ts` because Node's native TS stripping cannot resolve `.js`→`.ts` imports; the token parser is a separate function for later reuse.
